Chapter: CharEncodeBands

 char-encode was landed with nothing calling it, so this is its first
 exercise. Every non-ASCII character in codex/test was tier 0 when it was
 written, which is why no fixture in the tree had ever built a tier-1 or
 tier-2 unit and why the truncation in char-to-text survived two corrections
 (L-CONSTRUCT). The arms below straddle all four CCE band boundaries in both
 directions.

 The oracle is cce-decode-at, which is the other direction and separate code:
 length agreement alone would only compare char-encode against a function
 derived from the same spec.

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

Section: Probe

  rt : Integer -> Text
  rt (c) =
    let t = char-encode (code-to-char c)
   in let back = cce-decode-at t 0
   in show c & " len=" & show (text-length t) & " decoded=" & show back
      & (if text-length t == cce-encode-length c then " LEN-OK" else " LEN-BAD")
      & (if back == c then " RT-OK" else " RT-BAD")

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line (rt 0)
    print-line (rt 65)
    print-line (rt 127)
    print-line (rt 128)
    print-line (rt 192)
    print-line (rt 592)
    print-line (rt 2175)
    print-line (rt 2176)
    print-line (rt 41464)
    print-line (rt 67711)
    print-line (rt 67712)
    print-line (rt 100000)
  end

